    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it can.  This card's [When Digivolving] effect affects \"all of your opponent's Digimon,\" therefore it will also apply to opponent's Digimon that are newly played until the end of their turn.",
        "question": "This Digimon has [Leon Alexander] in its digivolution cards, and I activated its [When Digivolving] effect. Can it give ＜Security A. -1＞ to my opponent's Digimon that are played into the battle area afterward?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, that's correct.",
        "question": "If I have exactly 3 cards in my security stack, do I activate both the \"1 of your opponent's Digimon gets -6000 DP\" effect and <Recovery +1 (Deck)> when activating this card's [End of Your Turn] effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.  Once the [End of Your Turn] effect activates, you can perform the part of the effect after \"then\" regardless of the number of security cards.",
        "question": "When I have 3 security cards, can I use this card's [End of Your Turn] effect to gain <Recovery +1 (Deck)> and then use 1 of my Digimon to attack an opponent's Digimon if my security stack increases to 4 cards?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
